{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:60933e2eb73b5869424ecf69d90b96f339f85ff45ff143b7b9fe9b3e0ad8de56", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:60f5b232e47bb2f9f79da2a8673aedfb510879c539c0a6e7c9909ab032b2fed5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIt sometimes happens that a site <MATH_0001> does\nnot have a final object. In this case we define the\nglobal section functor as follows.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3761cdf761ef654273d5b944f56fc96c405967067284c9eed796e550acb12f22", "unit_id": "tag:06UM:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\Gamma(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{F}) =\n\\Mor_{\\textit{PSh}(\\mathcal{C})}(*, \\mathcal{F})\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$*$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-global-sections}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:009c51642bcfde6d9285b2157abeffb443fe72513cea837e68933a44057c332f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:00075947f9289734c7b0a926277e307bfc4221e47eac2fc68b640330a77cf323", "source_text": "The <TEXTITOPEN_0001>global sections<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> of a presheaf of sets <MATH_0001> over a\nsite <MATH_0002> is the set\n<MATH_0003>\nwhere <MATH_0004> is the final object in the category of presheaves on\n<MATH_0005>, i.e., the presheaf which associates to every object\na singleton.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:054611960ae0f2dd255453b434bb5351b8c74d60fac91194e187f7908d761fe0", "unit_id": "tag:06UN:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06UM", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4f291664334007fd021d57575bcb54182f7684948c831f254c2b61d664312206", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nOf course the same definition applies to sheaves as well.\nHere is one way to compute global sections.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:85173da5bfba36a3cc74f9431c00300bdfa438a915911ab6cdaea931d234199a", "unit_id": "tag:06UM:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$a, b : V \\to U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nh_V^\\# \\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r] & h_U^\\# \\ar[r] & {*}\n}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Gamma(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0007": "$a^*, b^* : \\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{F}(V)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-compute-global-sections}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:147a6523ae5dd5180705711ddb1708e6ca142dd9bff7ee083339fede9e126665", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c6d52c7f1206e9c6f2f75bc002a45736f0726f18560ba669dd553ee066b2b884", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002> be objects of <MATH_0003>\nsuch that\n<MATH_0004>\nis a coequalizer in <MATH_0005>. Then\n<MATH_0006> is the equalizer of\n<MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aa3ffbdece659226623f62fa57e31f05dce040995760cdb3e9d8b548b92e3697", "unit_id": "tag:0792:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Mor_{\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})}(h_U^\\#, \\mathcal{F}) = \\mathcal{F}(U)$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e0092555bd5eb5dc058e41ea3b6c5e87e25085c752871cfbbb43078244d09874", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2d45e9681d4c9da9e621ecf9686143402e6fbab26872e970658ed756c4b36566", "source_text": "Since <MATH_0001>\nthis is clear from the definitions.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:41b2746cc209de4512d10b87b0e6727aea12074faa27879e1569bcc478d5c8f6", "unit_id": "tag:0792:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\Sh(\\mathcal{D}) \\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nf^{-1} :\n\\Gamma(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{F})\n\\longrightarrow\n\\Gamma(\\mathcal{D}, f^{-1}\\mathcal{F})\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$f^{-1}$", "MATH_0006": "$*$", "MATH_0007": "$*$", "MATH_0008": "$s$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0011": "$s : * \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0012": "$f^{-1}s : * = f^{-1}* \\to f^{-1}\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0017": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\Gamma(\\mathcal{D}, f^{-1}\\mathcal{F}) \\to \\Gamma(\\mathcal{D}, \\mathcal{G})$", "MATH_0019": "$$\n\\Gamma(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{F})\n\\longrightarrow\n\\Gamma(\\mathcal{D}, \\mathcal{G})\n$$", "MATH_0020": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}) \\ar[rd]_h \\ar[rr]_f & &\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}) \\ar[ld]^g \\\\\n& \\Sh(\\mathcal{B})\n}\n$$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0023": "$$\nf^{-1} : g_*\\mathcal{F} \\longrightarrow h_*f^{-1}\\mathcal{F}\n$$", "MATH_0024": "$g_*f_*f^{-1}\\mathcal{F} = h_*f^{-1}\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0025": "$g_*$", "MATH_0026": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to f_*f^{-1}\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0027": "$g$", "MATH_0028": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0029": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0030": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0031": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0032": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0033": "$h_*$", "MATH_0034": "$f^{-1}\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0035": "$$\ng_*\\mathcal{F} \\longrightarrow h_*\\mathcal{G}\n$$", "MATH_0036": "$\\mathcal{B}$", "MATH_0037": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}) \\ar[d]_h \\ar[r]_f &\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}) \\ar[d]^g \\\\\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{B}) \\ar[r]^e & \\Sh(\\mathcal{A})\n}\n$$", "MATH_0038": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0039": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0040": "$$\ne^{-1}g_*\\mathcal{G} \\longrightarrow h_*f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}.\n$$", "MATH_0041": "$g_*\\mathcal{G} \\to e_*h_*f^{-1}\\mathcal{G} = (e \\circ h)_*f^{-1}\\mathcal{G}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0005": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0006": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0007": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0008": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0009": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:41c38570d0c17319dec02af1dabcc1392741af79f829871680c6a0f49eb1e848", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f4ca4f29af09f6364bc44abae0a4d0886088f3760b1927dcc3e276d04954b292", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNow, let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of topoi.\nThen for any sheaf <MATH_0002> on <MATH_0003> there is a pullback map\n<MATH_0004>\nNamely, as <MATH_0005> is exact it transforms <MATH_0006> into <MATH_0007>. Hence a global\nsection <MATH_0008> of <MATH_0009> over <MATH_0010>, which is a map\nof sheaves <MATH_0011>, can be pulled back to\n<MATH_0012>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nWe can generalize this a bit by considering a pair of sheaves\n<MATH_0013>, <MATH_0014> on <MATH_0015>, <MATH_0016>\ntogether with a map <MATH_0017>. Then we\ncompose the construction above with the obvious map\n<MATH_0018>\nto get a map\n<MATH_0019>\nThis map is sometimes also called a pullback map.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nA slightly more general construction which occurs frequently in nature\nis the following. Suppose that we have a commutative diagram of\nmorphisms of topoi\n<MATH_0020>\nNext, suppose that we have a sheaf <MATH_0021> on <MATH_0022>.\nThen there is a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>pullback map<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\n<MATH_0023>\nNamely, it is just the map coming from the identification\n<MATH_0024> together with\n<MATH_0025> applied to the canonical map <MATH_0026>.\nIf <MATH_0027> is the identity, then this map on global sections agrees \nwith the pullback map above.\n\n<STRUCT_0006><STRUCT_0007>\nIn the situation of the previous paragraph, suppose\nwe have a pair of sheaves <MATH_0028>, <MATH_0029>\non <MATH_0030>, <MATH_0031> together with a map\n<MATH_0032>, then we compose\nthe pullback map above with <MATH_0033> applied to\n<MATH_0034>\nto get a map\n<MATH_0035>\nRestricting to sections over an object of <MATH_0036> one recovers\nthe ``pullback map'' on global sections discussed above (with suitable\nchoices of sites).\n\n<STRUCT_0008><STRUCT_0009>\nAn even more general situation is where we have a commutative diagram of topoi\n<MATH_0037>\nand a sheaf <MATH_0038> on <MATH_0039>. Then there is a\n<TEXTITOPEN_0002>base change map<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>\n<MATH_0040>\nNamely, this map is adjoint to a map\n<MATH_0041>\nwhich is the pullback map just described.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a35618d47cbfd623c20d73f389a84f62b3291b892e42f9a4ff3106deba9d604e", "unit_id": "tag:06UM:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "06UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{B}') \\ar[r]_k \\ar[d]_{f'} &\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{B}) \\ar[d]^f \\\\\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}') \\ar[r]^l \\ar[d]_{g'} &\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}) \\ar[d]^g \\\\\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}') \\ar[r]^m &\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{D})\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "\\begin{align*}\nm^{-1} \\circ (g \\circ f)_*\n& =\nm^{-1} \\circ g_* \\circ f_* \\\\\n& \\to g'_* \\circ l^{-1} \\circ f_* \\\\\n& \\to g'_* \\circ f'_* \\circ k^{-1} \\\\\n& = (g' \\circ f')_* \\circ k^{-1}\n\\end{align*}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-compose-base-change}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c21bd1247e3e059555433de4a99556a777444a6dfced543cb3d20f2c2b6b58cb", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a04fd2821c74a9e2dec8f387ea8acd2f87f1f3831825e169c1c61a7b0ba1917f", "source_text": "Consider a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nof topoi. Then the base change maps for the two squares compose to give the\nbase change map for the outer rectangle. More precisely, the composition\n<MATH_0002>\nis the base change map for the rectangle. We omit the verification.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:095749ef53d32b99b7f53dc8f3973491470f181b8d90df39fc1eec7b2c823ff3", "unit_id": "tag:0F6X:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "06UM", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}'') \\ar[r]_{g'} \\ar[d]_{f''} &\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}') \\ar[r]_g \\ar[d]_{f'} &\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}) \\ar[d]^f \\\\\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}'') \\ar[r]^{h'} &\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{D}') \\ar[r]^h &\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{D})\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "\\begin{align*}\n(h \\circ h')^{-1} \\circ f_*\n& =\n(h')^{-1} \\circ h^{-1} \\circ f_* \\\\\n& \\to (h')^{-1} \\circ f'_* \\circ g^{-1} \\\\\n& \\to f''_* \\circ (g')^{-1} \\circ g^{-1} \\\\\n& = f''_* \\circ (g \\circ g')^{-1}\n\\end{align*}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-compose-base-change-horizontal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0738ed84480de77fdcdcc157150be54b5d2a263bace157f6764cc8f42365fe42", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2d47fb66c9c581b0064138e478470e52c3b7c3dcf45c3f8fcb5bf8509c62819f", "source_text": "Consider a commutative diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nof ringed topoi. Then the base change maps\nfor the two squares compose to give the base\nchange map for the outer rectangle. More precisely,\nthe composition\n<MATH_0002>\nis the base change map for the rectangle. We omit the verification.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b19200e7a72d81422bf6ea5199dab52c0b4f130df10fd5bd38157c379fe4ab17", "unit_id": "tag:0F6Y:statement"}
